audio:
  lang: en
  lines:
    'male|a||A state wants to know whether covering more low-income adults with Medicaid is worth what it costs: which design should answer that, and what must the answer become before it prices anything?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11720
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||The tempting answer is to rank the designs by prestige, a randomized trial first, and take the best one on offer.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1r2qcsu'
    'male|a||But you rarely get to choose: the design is handed to you by the way coverage happened to vary in your data.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1p20ami'
    male|a||If someone drew names at random, as Oregon did for Medicaid in 2008, you have a randomized trial, and the one promise is that the draw was random and both groups were followed alike.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:18awlpt'
    male|a||If something random only nudges people toward coverage, like a lottery win that merely lets you apply, that nudge is an instrument.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1m4shij'
    'male|a||Then you promise more: the nudge changes health only through coverage, and it never pushes anyone away from coverage.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:3tswf'
    'male|a||Which makes Oregon''s draw both at once: a trial of the invitation, and an instrument for coverage itself, and only the second reading needs those two extra promises.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:4xdtuk'
    male|a||If some states expanded Medicaid in 2014 and others did not, you compare their changes, a difference in differences, and promise both would have trended alike without it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:8vyqf8'
    male|a||If coverage jumps at a rule's cutoff, as Medicare does at sixty-five, you compare people just either side, and promise that nothing else jumps there too.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:uukr4f'
    male|a||If only one state changed, as California did with its 1988 tobacco tax, you weight other states into a blend that tracks it beforehand, and promise the blend would have kept tracking it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 23440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1sty1vg'
    male|a||And if all you have is who chose coverage, with their age, income and health, you compare like with like, and promise that nothing you did not measure still differs.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:lbcu2l'
    'male|a||Now read the promises in order: the first is kept by a coin, the last by nothing but your argument about what you measured.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:4ppw4v'
    male|a||So the rule is not the most prestigious design, but the one whose promise you can defend to someone who would like it to fail.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1qd9j5q'
    male|a||A new case. Heart-attack patients who live nearer a hospital with a catheter lab are more likely to get the procedure, and few people choose where to live for their heart. Click the design.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1dj60a5'
    male|a||A new case. Heart-attack patients who live nearer a hospital with a catheter lab are more likely to get the procedure, and few people choose where to live for their heart.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10800
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||An instrument: distance nudges who gets the procedure, as McClellan, McNeil and Newhouse used it in 1994, and the promise is that distance changes survival only through the procedure.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12920
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||And that promise is a hard one, because living near a big hospital may bring faster ambulances and other care as well.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8160
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||Whichever card you hold, what comes out is the same kind of thing: one number, for some people, in one place and time.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 16240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:szmuys'
    male|a||So take the strongest card, Oregon's lottery, and follow how much more must be argued before its number can price a policy.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1jo9u63'
    male|a||Oregon's lottery gives the cleanest number we have on what Medicaid does, but whose number is it?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8280
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||It comes from a lottery: in 2008 Oregon had room for about ten thousand more adults, so it drew about thirty thousand names from a list of about ninety thousand and invited them to apply.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1e5jgw0'
    male|a||For every hundred people drawn, about twenty-five more ended up covered than among a hundred people not drawn.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:12vw20t'
    'male|a||Those twenty-five are the compliers: the people whose coverage the draw itself switched on.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ucvqje'
    'male|a||The other seventy-five were not moved: most never enrolled, and a few would have been covered anyway, drawn or not.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:150k66y'
    male|a||So every Oregon estimate, scaled up from the draw, is an effect for that quarter, and only for them.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:tdxcyx'
    'male|a||Take one outcome that matters for a budget: visits to the emergency room.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:bfdga7'
    male|a||Over about eighteen months, coverage added about 0.41 visits per complier, with an interval from roughly 0.2 to 0.6.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:v6o1tl'
    male|a||On a base of about one visit, that is a rise of some forty percent, as Taubman and colleagues reported in 2014.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:sesz6u'
    male|a||But when Massachusetts extended coverage to nearly everyone in 2006, emergency visits there fell, by Sarah Miller's estimate; only the direction is drawn here.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:s3946n'
    male|a||Your call. The same kind of coverage raised emergency visits in Oregon and lowered them in Massachusetts. Which explanation fits what each number is?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1nd0z74'
    male|a||Each estimate belongs to the people its own reform moved, and those were different people.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5840
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||That is how Amanda Kowalski, writing in 2023, reads it: Oregon''s compliers were sicker than the people who never enrolled, drawn or not.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10760
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||She lets the effect change with how eager people were to enrol, a margin no one observes directly; Massachusetts's newly covered resemble Oregon's less eager, healthier people, and for them Oregon's estimates predict fewer emergency visits, not more.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 17880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:12rh2'
    male|a||So before Oregon's number can price an expansion anywhere else, three arguments have to be made.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:l69bad'
    male|a||First, the people your policy would cover must resemble Oregon's compliers, or be reweighted to them on things you can measure.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:17mg8kg'
    male|a||Second, the effect must not hinge on things you cannot measure, or you must model how it varies with them, as Kowalski did with eagerness to enrol.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1kmox9'
    male|a||Third, the setting must carry over, from Portland's clinics and prices in 2008 to your state today.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:wzwl3o'
    'male|a||None of the three can be checked in Oregon''s data: the lottery''s guarantee stops exactly where they begin.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1cmfsyb'
    'male|a||Suppose the number now belongs to the right people: a budget office still asks what each dollar buys.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||The simplest answer is a cost per outcome: the extra cost, call it delta C, divided by the change in the outcome, delta Y.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:kkhzg6'
    male|a||On the cost side, Finkelstein, Hendren and Luttmer put Oregon's Medicaid spending at about three thousand six hundred dollars per person-year.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:jc033t'
    male|a||But about sixty cents of each of those dollars paid for care the uninsured already got without paying, so the net cost, extra care plus bills people no longer paid themselves, is about fourteen hundred and fifty.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 13080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:2z7tee'
    male|a||On the outcome side, the share of people screening positive for depression fell by about nine points, from about thirty percent.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:dcao2a'
    male|a||Divide one by the other, and each person-year free of depression costs roughly sixteen thousand dollars, if all of the cost is charged to depression.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:fatpi9'
    male|a||That reading assumes the effect holds in every covered year; the nine points were measured after about two years, and if two years of coverage bought them, the price is about twice as high.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:m2046s'
    'male|a||But the nine points came with a range: anything from about two points to about seventeen fits the data.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1rqongr'
    male|a||Watch the price per case as the effect slides from one end of its range to the other.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1f930yx'
    male|a||At seventeen points the price falls under nine thousand dollars.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4200
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||At two, it climbs to about ninety thousand.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 3560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1v6o3tw'
    male|a||A ratio magnifies the uncertainty in its denominator, most of all when that denominator could lie close to zero.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1dnfvet'
    male|a||And three choices hide in this one division, none of them estimated by any design.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1qa69m5'
    male|a||Which cost? Count the full three thousand six hundred the state pays, and the price more than doubles, to about thirty-nine thousand.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ithrlx'
    male|a||Which outcome? Charging everything to depression ignores the fall in catastrophic medical bills, and the rise in diabetes diagnoses.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1axsbdd'
    male|a||And which yardstick? To set depression beside a hip replacement you convert it to quality-adjusted life years, with weights from surveys of how people value a year in that state.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:10qbs7p'
    male|a||Then a threshold, which someone has to choose, turns the price into a yes or a no.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1vfsfie'
    male|a||Sort the estimate from the choices. Which of these could a larger Oregon sample change?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1ir8ij9'
    male|a||Which of these could a larger Oregon sample change?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 3840
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||Only the range: more people shrink the sampling uncertainty, while the other two are choices no sample makes.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7080
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||So a cost per outcome is half estimate and half choice, and both halves can move it a long way.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8000
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||A price per case cannot say whether the same dollars would do more good elsewhere, so a second yardstick asks what a program is worth to the people who get it, per dollar it costs.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11880
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||Hendren and Sprung-Keyser call it the marginal value of public funds: W, what recipients would pay for the program, over C, its cost to the government net of anything it saves.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1lj5n8w'
    male|a||Above one, recipients value the program at more than it costs; below one, at less.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1awhhq8'
    male|a||For Oregon, Finkelstein, Hendren and Luttmer built W from the lottery's own estimates, of what coverage did to spending, to out-of-pocket bills and to health, since no one could simply be asked.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:zpf7g3'
    'male|a||Valuing each effect directly gives about sixteen hundred and seventy-five dollars a year, over a net cost of about fourteen hundred and fifty that counts the sixty cents as money the public gets back: a ratio of 1.16.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 24160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1kdewjb'
    male|a||That is Oregon's figure in Hendren and Sprung-Keyser's comparison of policies, with a ninety-five percent interval from 1.08 to 1.25.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:4gyphp'
    male|a||But a second approach, which infers the value from how recipients' other spending moves with their medical bills, gives seven hundred and ninety-three dollars, with a standard error of about four hundred.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:8m7s7n'
    male|a||That is a ratio near 0.55, with a range so wide it reaches from zero past one.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1b9y9m3'
    male|a||The interval around 1.16 is narrow; the distance between the two approaches is far wider, and no larger lottery would ever close it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:11b7mvu'
    'male|a||And the denominator hides a choice of its own: the state actually pays the full three thousand six hundred.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:dbce8s'
    male|a||Put that in the denominator and treat the sixty cents as worth nothing to anyone, and the ratio falls to about 0.47.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:fq6kms'
    male|a||But if whoever gets those sixty cents, the hospitals or poorer patients, values them dollar for dollar, they belong on top as well, and the ratio is back near one, at 1.06.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 20560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:199uz34'
    male|a||For comparison, Hendren estimated in 2016 that a dollar of the Earned Income Tax Credit is worth about ninety cents to the families who get it; his later work with Sprung-Keyser puts the 1993 expansion at 1.12.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 15240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1xljuzq'
    male|a||So whether Oregon's Medicaid beats a cash credit turns less on sampling error than on an approach and an incidence that someone has to argue.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:df943k'
    'male|a||And all of these figures leave out what Oregon was too small to see: effects on mortality and on most of physical health.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1erhfb7'
    male|a||Studies of the 2014 expansions, by Miller, Johnson and Wherry, found yearly mortality among low-income adults aged fifty-five to sixty-four fell by about 0.13 points, with a standard error of 0.05, roughly nine percent.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 17360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1ganmkv'
    male|a||If that holds, the value per dollar is understated; longer follow-up of the lottery's people, linked to death records, is what would settle it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:cs4g8z'
    male|a||One more case. A job program costs the government $1,000 per person. Recipients would pay $500 for it, and it later brings back $500 in extra taxes. What is its MVPF?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 14320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:er8bry'
    'male|a||One: recipients value it at five hundred, and after the extra taxes the government is out five hundred too.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7240
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||So which design should answer the state's question? The one whose promise you can defend, and a lottery makes that promise almost free.:
